und, dam, bastion, shelter”), from Proto-Germanic *hlaiwą. Compare the Westphalian placename Lünen. On the other hand, it seems clear that the similarity to the Polabian name of the town Glain, Glein, Chlein can hardly be coincidental. The Polabian might be from Germanic, but it has also been connected with Proto-Slavic *glina (“clay, loam”)."]],"senses":[[373876,"lüneburg","name","Lüneburg (a town in Lower Saxony, Germany; official name: Hansestadt Lüneburg)",0],[373877,"lüneburg","name","a rural district of Lower Saxony",1],[373878,"lüneburg","name","a farming community in eDumbe local municipality, Zululand district municipality, KwaZulu-Natal, South Africa",2],[373879,"lüneburg","name","a surname transferred from the place name",3]],"related_forms":[[55610,"lüneburg","lüneburgerin","derived"],[55611,"lüneburg","lüneburger","derived"],[55612,"lüneburg","lüneburgisch","derived"],[55613,"lüneburg","lüneburger heide","related"],[55614,"lüneburg","lünebach","related"],[55615,"lüneburg","limburg","related"]]},"rausten":{"entries":[["rausten",null,null,null]],"senses":[[645925,"rausten","adj","superlative degree of rau",0],[645926,"rausten","adj","inflection of rau:",1],[645927,"rausten","adj","strong genitive masculine/neuter singular superlative degree",2],[645928,"rausten","adj","weak/mixed genitive/dative all-gender singular superlative degree",3],[645929,"rausten","adj","strong/weak/mixed accusative masculine singular superlative degree",4],[645930,"rausten","adj","strong dative plural superlative degree",5],[645931,"rausten","adj","weak/mixed all-case plural superlative degree",6]],"inflections":[["rausten","rau","genitive,masculine,singular,strong,superlative,without-article"]]},"seherischste":{"entries":[["seherischste",null,null,null]],"senses":[[161731,"seherischste","adj","inflection of seherisch:",0],[161732,"seherischste","adj","strong/mixed nominative/accusative feminine singular superlative degree",1],[161733,"seherischste","adj","strong nominative/accus